Having ascended a Sporkhack barbarian in one or two tries, here's my
perspective on things.

On Feb 21, 1:40 pm, "3cnf...@gmail.com" <3cnf...@gmail.com> wrote:
> but I want to ascend one anyway. Having tried and failed three times,
> I think there's a fundamental flaw in my approach. My biggest
> questions for ascended barbarians are:
>
> 1. How do you circumvent the barbarian's weaknesses in ranged combat?
> I've tried bow/+6 poisoned arrows and hoarding pets in Sporkhack. For
> some reason, my pet purple worms seemed to die off far too quickly.
> Poisoned arrows worked nicely versus priests and soldiers, but I
> didn't use them on a regular basis.
>
> In Spork, this is a *far* more important question because of the
> "destroy armor" spell. When wearing a cloak of displacement,
> disenchanters, Rodney and spellcasters tore my AC down to -12 (from
> -36!).
>
> 2. Do you #twoweapon or use a two-hander such as Cleaver?
> In Sporkhack, it's nearly impossible to hit many enemies, such as arch-
> liches, Rodney, and named &, with basic #twoweapon or even basic
> single-weapon, so I've been using the Cleaver. However, when Cleaver
> got cursed in Moloch's sanctum, I rethought my approach.

In my Sporkhack ascensions (including one genoless wishless), I
haven't ever had problems with AC going down so drastically. Other
than the fact that you should really be wearing something with MC3
(robe/CoMR/CoProt), it sounds to me like you're just letting dangerous
enemies live too long, or facing too many at once. It's very possible
to kill stuff fast enough that destroy armor never becomes a
significant problem - most of my Sporkhack ascensions, I've only had
it cast on me two or three times.

Just always target the nasty casters first, and lure stuff away from
the rest of the gang if possible. And when you have the amulet don't
stop for anything unless its blocking the way. Even then, consider a
wand of teleport. You should be keeping _every_ wand of teleport you
run across, they're even more useful than they were in Vanilla.

I didn't carry anything ranged other than wands with my barbarian, and
never had any trouble with killing stuff quickly. I found Cleaver to
be very good, more than enough to mow through most things, even
Rodney, the high priest, and the demon lords. Sporkhack doubles the
damage bonus from strength when using a two-handed weapon, so with GoP
Cleaver goes from decent to far better than anything you can do with
basic #twoweapon.

In general, I've found that #twoweapon in Sporkhack is not worth it at
all unless you can at least get Skilled. Even then, you can have
problems hitting the toughest enemies. For a barbarian with access to
Cleaver, you should wish for GoP and then just make absolutely sure to
keep Cleaver blessed at all times.

> 3. What the hell did Belkar the barbarian do wrong?
> My hunch is that I'm just really bad at reacting to the status bar,
> but unsure.

As has been mentioned, the Statuscolors patch is really great, start
using it. If you're having problems with things getting cursed, you
may also want to turn on menucolors.

Other than that, it's hard to say without seeing your game
specifically. It may be that you're still wading into huge packs of
monsters still thinking that you can take them all in Sporkhack, or
otherwise not adjusting to the changes Sporkhack has made. You might
not be using all the resources available to you - always keep around a
few full healing potions, some panic scrolls (earth/cursed teleport/
blessed scare monster), and every teleport wand you find. Watch for
your HP dropping - if its going down quickly, don't just keep
fighting, either run or use up some of your emergency resources.

> 4. Should I just genocide liches?

Yes. Genoless is a significantly harder conduct in Sporkhack than in
Vanilla, for a variety of reasons, many of them specifically involving
liches. Genociding them is well worth it, and approaches necessity for
a not-too-strong character. It also only costs two blessed scrolls of
genocide - more than the one it takes in Vanilla, but still not so
bad.

